capability client/https-read-deadline  a time limit on an https:// response's reads
  heroes  http.send, http.Client.deadline_ms
  go      net/http.Client.Timeout over TLS
  rust    -
  python  requests' read timeout over TLS
  note    `tls.connect`'s deadline bounds the connection and its handshake, and what is left of the client's time limit is then set on the stream by `tls.set_deadline`, so every read and write of the exchange is bounded; a write it ends leaves the stream good for closing alone, which `send` does

