capability client/http2  an https:// request over HTTP/2 where the server's ALPN chooses h2, and several requests on one HTTP/2 connection the program holds
  heroes  http.send, http.round_trip_h2, http.to_h2_request, http.from_h2_response
  go      net/http.Transport's HTTP/2 (ForceAttemptHTTP2, TLSNextProto), net/http.Request.ProtoMajor as the client reads it
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    added 2026-11-18: the exchange is `http2`'s, its fields made HTTP/2's (names in lower case, HTTP/1.1's connection fields left out, Host as :authority), the response read back as an HTTP/1.1 one so redirects, retries, cookies and decoding hold; `send` still opens one connection a request, `round_trip_h2` keeps one; Python's standard library and requests speak HTTP/1.1 alone (httpx's http2=True is a third party's)

capability server/http2  a TLS server answering HTTP/2 where its listener offers h2 and the client chooses it
