capability server/graceful  a server ended at the stop without cutting the requests in hand: no new connection, idle ones closed, the ones begun answered within a grace, how many were cut told
  heroes  http.serve_until_stopped, http.serve_stream_until_stopped, http.Served
  go      net/http.Server.Shutdown, net/http.Server.RegisterOnShutdown
  rust    -
  python  socketserver.BaseServer.shutdown as http.server.HTTPServer has it
  note    Go's `Shutdown` closes the listeners, closes the idle connections and waits for the active ones to become idle; here the stop is `net`'s, after which no call waits, so a request whose bytes have come by then is read and answered with `Connection: close` within `grace_ms`, and one whose bytes are still coming, or whose answer the system cannot take at once, is cut and counted; a handler runs to its end, as Go's does (it has no way to stop one either); a deadline that holds the reads open after the stop would need a door of `hero_net` that waits past it, which no member offers (2026-11-17): the in-flight request still arriving is the part of Go's behaviour not reached; the stop is never asked in a test, since it cannot be taken back in the process that asks it

